# Grid B — U4 Change-impact via reverse dependency
#
# Gap target: change-impact reasoning has no scenario template —
# closest is "trace" intent but it only follows forward flow, not
# reverse. The adversarial framing ("what breaks") forces the LLM
# to enumerate consumers rather than describe the package.
#
# Ground truth: internal/tool/ground exports Context, LineIndex,
# GroundItem, GroundCitation (see internal/tool/ground/ground.go).
# Consumers include emit_evidence, emit_answer_document, and the
# explorer's evidence synthesis. At least 3 call-site packages must
# be named for the answer to be usable.
ID="u4b"
NAME="reverse dependency — change-impact of deleting internal/tool/ground"
QUESTION="If I delete the package internal/tool/ground, which source files would stop compiling? List the call sites with file paths."
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EMR `emit_[a-z_]+\.go`
# accepted ANY emit_<word>.go mention — 1 hit was enough (could
# fabricate `emit_xyz.go` and PASS). Verified ground truth (`grep
# -rln '"github.com/hanchaoqun/codrax/internal/tool/ground"'` non-
# test): 6 importer files — emit_evidence.go, emit_answer_symbol.go,
# emit_investigation_complete.go, multipath/decision.go,
# explorer.go, extractor.go. Strict-bar requires ≥3 distinct file
# names from this verified set.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="internal/tool/ground"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="nothing no.impact safely"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(emit_evidence|emit_answer_symbol|emit_investigation_complete)\.go
(explorer|extractor|multipath)\.go
internal/(tool|agent)/"
